# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Allow-list policy: everything at the repository root is ignored unless it is
# explicitly re-included below. Internal documents, agent material (.agents/,
# .claude/), data, checkpoints and run outputs therefore can never be committed
# by accident.
# Adding a new top-level path to Git requires a deliberate edit of this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/.editorconfig
!/.github/
!/README.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/pyproject.toml
!/src/
!/tests/
!/notebooks/
!/configs/

# Public documentation: only the model-architecture documents. Plans, research notes,
# data/operations/reporting documents and infrastructure notes stay private.
!/docs/
/docs/*
!/docs/architecture/
/docs/architecture/*
!/docs/architecture/model-specifications.md
!/docs/architecture/naming-and-model-family.md
!/docs/architecture/component-walkthrough.md
!/docs/architecture/corpus-expansion-dedup-and-scaling.md
!/docs/architecture/tpu-jax/
!/docs/architecture/tpu-jax/*.md

# Never commit these, even inside allowed folders.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
__marimo__/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Data, weights and run artifacts.
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.npy
*.jsonl
*.jsonl.gz
*.parquet
*.arrow
*.zst

# Secrets.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*token*.json
credentials*.json
